# yours.list — your files, the ones `vikix snapshot` keeps a history of.
#
# Paths are relative to your home folder. A folder means everything in
# it, apart from what the exclude list in bin/vikix leaves out (Vikix's
# own links in ~/.stumpwm.d, logs, backups). With this history, any
# change to these files, by you or by an AI agent, can be seen with
# `vikix changes` and taken back with `vikix undo`.

.stumpwm.d                  # user.lisp, and any Lisp files of your own
.config/alacritty
.config/picom
.config/dunst
.config/rofi
.config/vikix/keyboard
.config/vikix/wallpaper      # the wallpaper you chose (a link to it)
.config/gammastep            # night light times and colours
.config/mimeapps.list
.config/vikix/backup          # where backups go (not the password: that stays out of here)
.config/vikix/backup-exclude  # what they leave out
.config/vikix/optional        # optional features you chose (vikix windows setup)
.config/vikix/windows         # where the Windows VM's disk is
.Xresources
.bashrc
.bash_profile
